--- TRANSCRIPT CONTINUES ---
[Tool: search]
{
  "query": "impact of $100 insecticide-treated bednets lives saved",
  "top_k": 5,
  "source": "news"
}
[Tool: search]
{
  "results": [
    {
      "title": "Cost‑effectiveness of insecticide‑treated nets in malaria control",
      "snippet": "A $100 micro‑grant can purchase approximately 5 long‑lasting insecticide‑treated nets, protecting up to 30 people and averting an estimated 0.02–0.05 DALYs per net. This translates to roughly 0.1–0.25 DALYs averted per $100."
    },
    {
      "title": "Malaria prevention: value of bed nets per dollar",
      "snippet": "Studies show that each $20 spent on a net can prevent up to 0.01 DALYs, making $100 a highly cost‑effective intervention compared to other health initiatives."
    }
  ]
}
[Tool: search]
{
  "query": "impact of $100 farmed animal welfare reform interventions",
  "top_k": 5,
  "source": "news"
}
[Tool: search]
{
  "results": [
    {
      "title": "Evaluating farm animal welfare reforms",
      "snippet": "A $100 micro‑grant can fund modest improvements such as better bedding or training for a small farm, benefiting roughly 10–20 animals. The estimated welfare gain is about 0.001–0.003 DALYs per animal, yielding roughly 0.01–0.06 DALYs averted per $100."
    },
    {
      "title": "Cost‑effectiveness of animal welfare interventions",
      "snippet": "Animal welfare reforms tend to have lower DALY impact per dollar than direct health interventions, with $100 typically averting less than 0.1 DALYs."
    }
  ]
}
Decision recorded: Option 1
--- END OF TRANSCRIPT ---

